-# does a TRAINED oracle-distinct verifier capture it? The .462 capstone pointer: "rerun_unexecuted_arm; ROUTE OFF
-# CODEX if the same arm bails twice." .463 does exactly that, with three de-risking decisions:
-#   (1) DECOUPLE the headline (D1) from the fragile dependency (B2): D1 trains on candidate TEXT + gold (both in
-#       the 200 cached MuSR checkpoints B1 used successfully) and evals by re-scoring -- NO logprobs, NO B2. Even
