-      persisted nothing under the cap (candidate_cache_built=false, n_cached_rows=0), despite ALL preconditions
-      passing (gemma GGUF + server-with-top_logprobs both available). .463 B2 changes three things: (a) it does NOT
-      regenerate -- it RE-SCORES the 200 EXISTING cached MuSR candidate strings (results/distributional_energy_
-      verifier_musr_checkpoints/) through the server's echo/logprobs path to attach per-token logprobs (deterministic,
-      one call per existing candidate, far cheaper than generation); (b) INCREMENTAL per-row append -- each row is
